    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34304" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕcūlor</span></b> ,
		āri, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i> [peculium], <i>to
				defraud the public</i>, <i>to embezzle the public
				money</i>, <i>to peculate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rem publicam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					3, 17, 3</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕcūlans</span></b> , antis,
				P. a.—As <i>subst. plur.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕcūlantĭa</span></b> ,
			ium, n., <i>peculations</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Commod. 70, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
